	(text "U8 HPI (I2C, address 0x08, 3.3 V only, p.5) is not on I2C_INT: U8 has no supply without\nUSB \"Power\" and Infineon does not document its HPI pins unpowered. They float; TP3/TP4\ngive access. If they ever need pull-ups: to U8's own VDDD, never to +3.3V_MCU"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 222.25 111.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
				(color 120 40 200 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0a870e1b-74cf-409a-aadc-eb81ddd1ed9f")
	)
	(text "12 V target: PD's standard voltages are 5/9/15/20 V (Infineon KBA231336), so a charger\nwithout 12 V gives at most 9 V at 3 A (27 W). 15 V needs R71 5.1k, R12 24.9k, R78 8.2k:\nwith today's R12/R78, IC2 cuts USB \"Power\" at ~14 V, even if I2C requests 15 V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 222.25 106.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
				(color 194 0 122 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "14ede3ec-693f-49f9-8ebf-1514f2e9a083")
	)
	(text "Bring-up: U8 is only documented with a VBUS switch. Check that it still negotiates 12 V\nwith VDC_OUT on VBUS and that chargers keep VBUS when the board draws > 2.5 W during\nthe 5 V -> 12 V step. Also try a charger with 12 V below 3 A: Infineon doesn't document\n9 V vs the 5 V fallback. Check that U8 behaves with its HPI pins floating"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 222.25 125.73 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
				(color 210 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3922c382-a90e-462f-903b-7593afb55b55")
	)
	(text "U8 VDDD"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 230.632 23.114 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(color 230 100 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "42d5b120-cb1a-4a09-8ae0-3faf5141e5d9")
	)
	(text "U8 VBUS_IN"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 230.632 35.814 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(color 230 100 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6e3ee450-7907-46cb-9cbb-04a910eaa021")
	)
	(text "To keep the BOM small, I am using 887k as a shield resistor (and not 1M)\nsince the HD3SS3220 wants 880-910k on VBUS_DET and I dont want to risk using a 1M there"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 47.752 151.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.5 0.5)
				(color 194 0 122 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8594677b-eba5-4aba-9103-bcdb43cef8e1")
	)
	(text "Output of internal 3.3-V regulator"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196.088 36.576 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
				(color 100 100 100 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "88d23383-e333-4f20-b67b-75fde382b255")
	)
	(text "USB Port \"Power\""
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.573 14.478 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "958107cc-41fc-4049-9133-0208b2af2afe")
	)
	(text "No VBUS switch (no room for a PFET): VDC_OUT sits on VBUS and VBUS_FET_EN is open,\nso the board loads VBUS from the first 5 V. Overvoltage is cut at IC2 instead:\nOV1 ladder R11/R12/R78 on Power Mux"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 222.25 101.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
				(color 194 0 122 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9e05de99-4e78-4683-942d-0b9d5a4fe7ee")
	)
	(text "U8 CYPD3177 (EZ-PD BCR): resistors set the voltage window, no NVM to program.\nVBUS_MIN = GND (5 V), VBUS_MAX 5.1k/2.4k (12 V), ISNK_COARSE 5.1k/5.1k (3 A),\nISNK_FINE = GND (Tables 2-4, p.10). It requests the highest PDO in 5-12 V:\n12 V, else 9 V, else 5 V. D+/D-/DNU open, FLIP open = data capable (p.7)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 222.25 95.25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
				(color 194 0 122 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "aaa3cbba-5827-4053-bf4e-68dee9577f87")
	)
	(text "22V surge protection"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 88.646 34.036 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "af5887fc-439c-47a5-8d62-855d0d1fd0ce")
	)
	(text "C3 + C41/C47 on VDDD (1 uF + 2x 100 nF), C4 on VCCD (1 uF): CYPD3177 Table 1, p.8"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.352 17.272 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
				(color 194 0 122 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b86c93a1-eb83-470a-8a83-dc22eb6851ca")
	)
	(text "USB UFP / Sink 12V/3A = 36W"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 193.04 113.03 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "c3626ce0-e2a2-417f-ba12-8407cd89a564")
	)
	(text "U8 VDDD"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.392 23.114 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(color 230 100 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e594f6ad-4bac-4845-981f-23622a7d1bdf")
	)
	(text "If no offer fits 5-12 V at 3 A, U8 falls back to 5 V (p.11). VBUS stays on the board\n(FAULT, SAFE_PWR_EN open) and firmware cannot read U8: check the input voltage on the\npower module (INA4230) before enabling the FPGA rails and treat 5 V as low power"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 222.25 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
				(color 120 40 200 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e6e4c9ac-c18f-4a74-bf63-3562d08ab9e3")
	)
